          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Chief Justice Rehnquist, chief Justice Rehnquist opened the argument."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice (unspecified)",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "97c6498b642d9972ab0b099d0d504cd1760391bc30c03fbee2d51ef7006909fb",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-97c6498b642d-0000-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice (unspecified), according to Justice (unspecified), a Justice asked whether the provision requiring material to be objectionable to minors constitutes a national standard."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "97c6498b642d9972ab0b099d0d504cd1760391bc30c03fbee2d51ef7006909fb",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-97c6498b642d-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 20,
              "start": 20
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice, a Justice inquired whether Congress considered that foreign providers could circumvent the law."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "General Olson",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "97c6498b642d9972ab0b099d0d504cd1760391bc30c03fbee2d51ef7006909fb",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-97c6498b642d-0001-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 21,
              "start": 20
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "General Olson responded that Congress explicitly considered foreign commerce and would prosecute where possible."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "97c6498b642d9972ab0b099d0d504cd1760391bc30c03fbee2d51ef7006909fb",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-97c6498b642d-0001-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 31,
              "start": 31
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "A Justice asked whether the appellate court properly barred enforcement on First Amendment grounds because the statute relies on community standards."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "97c6498b642d9972ab0b099d0d504cd1760391bc30c03fbee2d51ef7006909fb",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-97c6498b642d-0003-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 52,
              "start": 52
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Stevens, the screens already exist."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Opponents",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "97c6498b642d9972ab0b099d0d504cd1760391bc30c03fbee2d51ef7006909fb",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-97c6498b642d-0003-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 52,
              "start": 52
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Opponents claimed the statute is intrusive, expensive, and burdensome."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Government",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "97c6498b642d9972ab0b099d0d504cd1760391bc30c03fbee2d51ef7006909fb",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-97c6498b642d-0003-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 53,
              "start": 53
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Government argued the statute is less intrusive."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "97c6498b642d9972ab0b099d0d504cd1760391bc30c03fbee2d51ef7006909fb",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-97c6498b642d-0003-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 53,
              "start": 53
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Court stated that affirming the Third Circuit\u2019s decision would place obscene material in front of children."
      }
